# VehiclePositions feeds to archive, one vp-poller@<id> unit per row; an
# agency without a row runs no VP poller. Every id must also be an
# agencies.tsv row: reconcile-r2.sh reports a vp/<id>/ archive of any other
# id as an orphan.
# The collection is a bounded validation window: the feeds' predicted delays
# (TripUpdates) are compared with where the buses actually were. Nothing in
# the app ingests these samples. When the window ends, disable the units and
# delete the rows (MIGRATION.md, "VehiclePositions validation window").
# 20s, not the 60s TripUpdate poll: a stop passage is reconstructed from
# positions near the stop, so its time is only as fine as the poll interval,
# and a window of days keeps the extra volume bounded.
# The mcapps.jp file is vehicle_position.bin, singular.
# id	name	interval	url
8	hiroden	20	https://ajt-mobusta-gtfs.mcapps.jp/realtime/8/vehicle_position.bin
9	hirobus	20	https://ajt-mobusta-gtfs.mcapps.jp/realtime/9/vehicle_position.bin
10	hiroko	20	https://ajt-mobusta-gtfs.mcapps.jp/realtime/10/vehicle_position.bin
